dot -Tsvg  architecture.dot -o architecture.svg

first_login.png and status_cluster.png show the backend in a local,
isolated demo installation.
first_metric.png and archived_job.png show synthetic cpu_load samples for
demo_cluster, node001 and demo job 1001. No production data or credentials
were used. The corresponding DE/EN chapters provide text alternatives.

node_overview.png, first_metric_overview.png and running_job.png were captured
from official backend 1.5.4 with synthetic node states, measurements and jobs.
They show demo_cluster, node001/first_subcluster and node002/second_subcluster;
job 1002 is running. No Slurm cluster or production installation is involved.
The full node view supplies the navigation and identity context missing from
the smaller first_metric.png detail. The guide explains the relevant controls
and distinguishes this demonstration from a real scheduler integration test.

Reproduction from the repository root, with requirements-test.txt installed:

python3 tests/capture_docs_ui.py --source . \
  --backend-dir /path/to/unpacked/backend-1.5.4 \
  --work /path/to/new/private/capture-directory \
  --browser-executable /path/to/chromium

The backend directory must contain the official cc-backend and gen-keypair
binaries. The capture tool refuses an existing work directory, binds loopback,
blocks external browser requests and stops its backend at the end. It leaves
generated credentials and logs in the private work directory. Only files from
its screenshots/ subdirectory belong in this image directory; evidence.json
records the synthetic identities and verified job states.

metric_flow.de.svg and metric_flow.en.svg explain the path of a single metric.
Their editable Graphviz sources are metric_flow.de.dot and metric_flow.en.dot:

dot -Tsvg docs/img/metric_flow.de.dot -o docs/img/metric_flow.de.svg
dot -Tsvg docs/img/metric_flow.en.dot -o docs/img/metric_flow.en.svg
